        "The full historical three-file diff replaces removed Places setAndFetchFaviconForPage calls in tabs and feeds with Thunderbird-owned fetching and explicit Places storage. specialTabs.setFavIcon becomes async and awaits MailUtils.setFaviconForPage before updating the tab display. The new MailUtils helper distinguishes pageURI, iconURI and fetched dataURI, handles data icons directly, skips known cached image data and logs exceptions. Its historical network branch calls the async converter without await; the fixed accepted helper now awaits conversion/storage and restricts page identities to http(s). Later completion/retrieval changes987/993/996 belong to their own audits, not this historical patch.",
        "The historical feed path registers feedURL in Places history, obtains icon image data through the shared converter, waits for storage callback and retrieves the stored URI. Accepted FeedUtils now discovers an icon, validates fetched image MIME type, inserts the feed page, awaits storage, handles rejected/corrupt data with a warning and empty return, and uses getFaviconForPage. The old setAndFetch comment is historical wording rather than evidence that the removed API is still used. The inspected tab event caller starts setFavIcon without awaiting it; that caller boundary remains explicit.",
        "The channel helper uses the system principal, inherited CORS context, chrome allowance, script disallowance and internal favicon policy. It rejects failed fetch status, reads the stream, closes it, converts image bytes through Blob/FileReader and resolves an nsIURI data URL; exceptions reject. The landed historical diff uses resolver.reject on the failed-fetch path, matching mkmelin’s requested correction despite the actual review thread remaining Not Done. These named flags are observed contracts, not a tested claim that every request is secure. The async helper returns a promise even though its retained JSDoc names nsIURI.",
        "Complete Bug1922849 reports every mochitest failing at startup after the upstream API removal, then records landing and unaffected beta/ESR flags. Upstream Bug1894633 comments0–13 explain separating Places storage from network fetching for privacy/security, describe the proposed DB/fetch/store split and eventual dependency breakdown, then record initial landing, requested CLOSED TREE backout and reland. The backout cause beyond that request and linked upstream implementations were not independently inspected.",
        "D224617 explains copying the network helper because upstream exposes it only in test utilities. Tobyp accepts while explicitly not running tests; the author later requests renewed review after extra changes. Mkmelin accepts and promises the reject adjustment, which is present in the actual landed diff. Daisuke later describes a planned callback-to-Promise API change. Two Try links and those historical review reports do not establish a newly executed result.",
        "The previously withdrawn byte-corruption hypothesis stays withdrawn: the exact clean local NetUtil419–456 record returns ArrayBuffer, so constructing Uint8ClampedArray from that value is not evidence of byte-string corruption. That Gecko revision is dependency context and was not established as paired with the fixed comm endpoint; it is excluded from fixed accepted comm currentChecks. Existing dataflow and channel-contract lessons are reused with their original checked quotes, without duplicating followup chronology."
